      "text": [
        ": «خَمْسَةٌ لاَ يَنَامُونَ اَلْهَامُّ بِدَمٍ يَسْفِكُهُ وَ ذُو اَلْمَالِ اَلْكَثِيرِ لاَ أَمِينَ لَهُ وَ اَلْقَائِلُ فِي اَلنَّاسِ اَلزُّورَ وَ اَلْبُهْتَانَ عَنْ عَرَضٍ مِنَ اَلدُّنْيَا يَنَالُهُ وَ اَلْمَأْخُوذُ بِالْمَالِ اَلْكَثِيرِ وَ لاَ مَالَ لَهُ وَ اَلْمُحِبُّ حَبِيباً يَتَوَقَّعُ فِرَاقَهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1446 - Abu Basir narrated from Imam Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) who said:\n\"There are five types of people who cannot sleep: one who is anxious about shedding blood, the possessor of a great amount of wealth who lacks a trustworthy guardian, one who spreads lies and false accusations among people to gain a worldly benefit, the person burdened with a large amount of wealth but has none himself, and one who deeply loves someone and fears separation from them.\""
        ]
      }
